## 6. Investigation Tools and Log Sources

The following AWS services and log sources help investigate GuardDuty findings.

| AWS Service | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Amazon GuardDuty | Detect suspicious activities and generate findings |
| AWS CloudTrail | Investigate API calls and account activities |
| VPC Flow Logs | Analyze network traffic |
| Amazon CloudWatch | Monitor logs, metrics, and alerts |
| AWS Security Hub | Centralize and prioritize security findings |
| AWS Config | Review resource configuration changes |
| Amazon S3 Data Events | Investigate S3 object-level activities |
| Amazon Inspector | Identify software vulnerabilities |

### Important Log Files

For Linux-based EC2 instances:

**Authentication logs:**

```bash
/var/log/secure
```

**System logs:**

```bash
/var/log/messages
```

These logs can help investigate authentication attempts and system-level activities.

